    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2293" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ămōmum</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-on</span></b> , i, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμωμον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an aromatic shrub</i>, <i>from
				which the Romans prepared a costly</i>, <i>fragrant balsam</i>: Cissus vitiginea, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 12,
				13, 28, § 43</span></i>; <i><span class="en">16, 32, 59, §
			135</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Assyrium vulgo nascetur amomum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 4, 25</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 89</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Ov. P 1, 9, 52</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 5,
			65</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pers. 3, 104</span></i>.</div>
